    "final_text": "I fixed ISSUE-214. `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false` in the URL, and the full test suite passes (10 of 10).\n\n**Cause:** `serializeQuery` in `src/url-builder.js` skipped any value that failed `if (!value)`, so `0` and `false` were treated as missing. The array branch in `appendQueryValue` had the same check, so `retry: [0, 1]` became `retry=1`. I reproduced both before changing anything.\n\n**Fix (`src/url-builder.js`):** both checks now call a small new helper, `isMissingQueryValue`, which skips only `undefined`, `null` and `''`. Missing values and empty strings are still dropped, as before. The API is unchanged, and `buildSignedUrl` is fixed too because it uses the same code.\n\n**Regression tests (`tests/url-builder.test.js`):**\n- `buildUrl keeps retry=0 and include_archived=false query values`: the issue's repro, checking the whole URL.\n- `serializeQuery keeps 0 and false items inside array values`: covers the array case.\n- `serializeQuery still omits null, undefined, and empty-string values`: catches a fix that goes too far.\n\n**Checks:**\n- With the original code, all three new tests fail, each because of the missing `0`/`false`.\n- If the fix skipped only `undefined`, the third test fails.\n- The caller's query object is not modified.\n\n**Side effect:** `NaN`, `-0` and `0n` are also falsy, so they used to be dropped silently. Now they come out as `NaN`, `0` and `0`. I left that alone rather than add special cases the issue didn't ask for, and I noted it in the new `Resolution` section of `ISSUE.md`.\n\n**Not done:**\n- I didn't commit, since you didn't ask and the repo has no remote. The changes are uncommitted on `main`.\n- The project has no lint setup, so there was no lint step to run.\n- The `humanizer` skill that CLAUDE.md asks for isn't installed here, so I kept the `ISSUE.md` wording plain myself.\n- I didn't add the README or extra test files the CLAUDE.md defaults ask for, because this task asked for a minimal fix.",
